tests/ir/no_ir_array_literal.sky:6:5: note: `K⁻¹ @ f` is rewritten to a Cholesky solve
  |
6 | u = K⁻¹ @ f
  |     ^^^^^^^
  |     - positive definite
  = note: rewrite `K⁻¹ @ f` to a Cholesky solve: K is Matrix[2,2] and PositiveDefinite, f is Vector[2]. Factor K = L·Lᵀ (L lower-triangular), solve L·y = f, then Lᵀ·x = y. x = K⁻¹·f is Vector[2], and K⁻¹ is never formed.
